- cxx-mixed-designated-initializer: quickjs.h's JSCFunctionListEntry-building
  macros (JS_CFUNC_DEF and the 15 others alongside it) each build a
  brace-enclosed initializer that mixes positional clauses (name, prop_flags,
  def_type, magic) with a designated clause (.u = {...}) in the same
  brace-enclosed list. C allows that mix; C++ (P1975/P0329) requires a list
  to be either fully positional or fully designated, so g++/clang++ reject
  every one of these macros with "either all initializer clauses should be
  designated or none of them should be". Confirmed under g++ -std=c++20 on
  both quickjs-2026-06-04 and quickjs-2025-09-13. Fixed via
  patches/004-cxx-designated.patch (designates all five outer fields; the
  nested .u = {...} content is left positional since it's internally
  consistent on its own).

    // any use of a JS_CFUNC_DEF-family macro in a .cpp translation unit,
    // e.g. quickjs-libc.c's JSCFunctionListEntry tables compiled as C++:
    static const JSCFunctionListEntry proto_funcs[] = {
        JS_CFUNC_DEF("foo", 0, js_foo),
    };
    // g++ -std=c++20: error: either all initializer clauses should be
    // designated or none of them should be

- config-debugger-always-required: the CMake option CONFIG_DEBUGGER (default
  ON, but was OFF for WASI/EMSCRIPTEN builds before this fix) controls only
  whether defs.cmake adds quickjs-debugger.c and
  quickjs-debugger-transport-*.c to QUICKJS_SOURCES. quickjs.c itself calls
  js_debugger_check(), js_debugger_exception(), js_debugger_free(),
  js_debugger_free_context() and js_debugger_new_context() unconditionally
  (no #ifdef CONFIG_DEBUGGER around the call sites in quickjs.c), so
  building with CONFIG_DEBUGGER=OFF always fails at link time with undefined
  symbols, on every platform, not just wasm. Found while adding Emscripten
  support: CMakeLists.txt defaulted CONFIG_DEBUGGER to OFF for
  WASI/EMSCRIPTEN, which broke the link; changed the wasm-target default
  back to ON as a build-system-level workaround (see CMakeLists.txt), but
  the root cause (missing #ifdef guards in quickjs.c) is still present and
  CONFIG_DEBUGGER=OFF remains broken for every target, including native.

    cmake -B build -DCONFIG_DEBUGGER=OFF && cmake --build build --target qjs
    # wasm-ld/ld: undefined symbol: js_debugger_check (and 4 related symbols)

